        "id": "XfoAueJtQBeQ"
      },
      "source": [
        "4. MLP Architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "* Lecture given: the basic RNN updates $h_t = h(Ux_t + Wh_{t-1} + b)$\n",
        "\n",
        "* An MLP removes the recurrence ($W = 0$) and stacks multiple layers:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$h^{(1)} = \\text{ReLU}(W^{(1)} x + b^{(1)}), \\quad\n",
        "h^{(2)} = \\text{ReLU}(W^{(2)} h^{(1)} + b^{(2)}), \\quad\n",
        "\\hat y = W^{(3)} h^{(2)} + b^{(3)}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "* Activation: we use ReLU rather than sigmoid/tanh because\n",
        "ReLU does not saturate for positive inputs, mitigating the vanishing-gradient problem\n",
        "\n",
        "* Regularisation: Dropout layers randomly zero\n",
        "out hidden units during training, preventing overfitting on the small training set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "JsTpABVMQzCF",
